  "walkthrough": [
    "Goal: draw quick, sweeping lines and see them as smooth curves however close I zoom in, never as straight pieces with corners between the pen's samples.",
    "Entry: a screen-size canvas at fit with the Ink Pen (the default brush, black). Flick a fast loop and a fast S-curve: the pen reports a sample only every 30 to 50 canvas pixels at that speed, and Android adds one of its own on the straight line between two of them every frame.",
    "What appears: each line follows one smooth curve through the pen's samples, its width changing evenly with the pressure; the frame samples Android adds on the straight chord are no corners. While the pen moves, the last bit of the line behind the tip may bend a little as the next samples arrive; once the pen lifts the line stays exactly as it was last drawn.",
    "Zoomed in with two fingers to 8x on a turn, the edges stay round: no straight pieces, no corners, no thinner spots where pieces meet. The Pencil's graphite lays as evenly along a fast curve as along a slow one.",
    "Drawing a fast curve while zoomed in at 8x is smooth under the tip and when lifted. Undo takes it back at once; redo returns it.",
    "Nothing changes in the files: old strokes, drawn before, now show as curves too, and the artwork reopens exactly as it was drawn. A quick inward pinch fits the canvas again."
  ],
